    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0983" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/525: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Argentina</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)<anchor n="27" xml:id="d702-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-11T18:00:00-04:00">May 11, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Formal action is to be taken May 13 by the Commission of Inquiry and
                    Conciliation, Bolivia and Paraguay, with regard to the repatriation of
                    prisoners. The plan will probably call for the services of the Military Attaché
                    at your mission. Please ask him to be ready.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d702-f1" n="27" type="source" xml:id="d702-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date to the
                    Ambassador in Brazil as telegram No. 15.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
